class.description:
A [CgameMotionMatchingDatabase] stores per-frame feature vectors for a set of animation clips and answers "which clip and frame best matches this query" questions. It is consumed by [AnimationNodeMotionMatching] but can also be used from scripts directly.
Each frame is described by a 24 dimensional feature vector: root velocity (2), root facing (1), three trajectory samples at 0.2, 0.4 and 0.6 seconds (position x/y and facing, 9), left/right foot position (6) and left/right foot velocity (6). Features are normalized by their mean and standard deviation and scaled by per-group [member weights].
[method build] creates a k-means bucket index with triangle-inequality pruning, so [method search] returns exactly the same result as [method brute_force_search] while visiting far fewer frames. A [member continue_bias] below [code]1.0[/code] makes the frame that follows the currently playing one cheaper, which keeps playback stable.
[codeblock]
var db := CgameMotionMatchingDatabase.build_default_database()
var query := db.query_from(velocity, facing, desired_velocity, desired_facing, lf, rf, lv, rv)
var result := db.search(query, current_clip, current_frame)
print(result.clip, " ", result.frame, " ", result.cost)
[/codeblock]
A query is a [Dictionary] holding either a [code]features[/code] [PackedFloat32Array] with [constant DIMS] floats, or the frame fields accepted by [method frame_features]. Search results are dictionaries with [code]clip[/code], [code]frame[/code], [code]cost[/code] and [code]continuing[/code] keys.
